 ry of Indigenous Slavery in U.S. History
LOCATION:Boston Public Library\, 700 Boylston Street\, Boston\, MA 02116
DESCRIPTION:Join author Linford Fisher in a discussion of his book\, Steali
 ng America\, where he shows that although the first enslaved Africans arri
 ved in Jamestown in 1619\, European slavery in America began more than a c
 entury before.\nhttps://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5e8c9ef213992f00c5b
 6a6\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
