SUMMARY:Author Talk — Alex Krieger: Greenhorn
LOCATION:Jamaica Plain Library\, 30 South Street\, Jamaica Plain\, MA 02130
DESCRIPTION:Join local author Alex Krieger as he reads from and discusses h
 is new memoir Greenhorn: Episodes in an Immigrant's Life. It explores a li
 fe shaped by motion\, memory\, cultures and careers\, which unfolds in the
  art of making a home in the unfamiliar. At the age of nine\, Alex Krieger
  arrived in America with his three parents—survivors of the Holocaust. I
 n Chicago\, he finds his fourth first-grade classroom to learn a fourth la
 nguage in four years. From displaced childhood\, the journeying continues 
 as teacher\, architect\, planner of cities. With a poet's sensitivity and 
 a craftsman's precision\, Krieger reflects on that greenhorn's instinct to
  embrace the values of an adopted nation while remaining eyewitness to par
 adoxes.\nhttps://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ad26ad6fee2d21deb23b8a7\nFr
 om Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ad26ad6fee2d21deb23b8a7
END:VEVENT
